oor open. “control.” i keep the"], ["i rub my greasy fingertips together. “three failures,” i say. i lay the rusted key beside the other two. “not the same wrong.” i change one tooth, then try once more. if it fails, evidence.", "three tries. i rub my greasy fingertips together. “failure,” i mutter, then pocket the rusted key. “one wrong guess, maybe.” i keep the key in my pocket, but it’s not the same kind of key. i keep the rusted key in my pocket, too. it’s a pattern, maybe. i keep the rusted key in my pocket, but it’s not the same kind of key."], ["i rub my fingertips together. “minor,” i say. i keep the paper, but leave the tear visible. i move one folded scrap beside it. “still wrong,” i say. “useful later, maybe.”", "i rub my fingertips together. minor. minor. i keep the paper, but the paper is still wrong. i keep the paper. minor. i keep the paper. i rub my fingertips together again. minor. i keep the paper. minor. i keep the paper."], ["i stop halfway. i rub my greasy fingertips together. “lost.” i take the plan from my pocket, but not the goal. i look at the first tool. “the first thing,” i say. i start there.", "halfway. lost. i rub my greasy fingertips together. lost. i keep the plan in my pocket, but the goal is still there. i pocket the plan and keep the pocket. lost means the plan was meant to be kept."], ["i hold the broken piece against the light. “one wrong pocket,” i say. i mark the failed spot with a bolt, then make one smaller patch. if it fails again, i keep the evidence. i try.", "i rub my greasy fingertips together. “mistake. mistake.” i hold the broken piece against the light. “one wrong click, one wrong pocket. i keep the wrong pocket.” i pocket the broken piece and keep the wrong pocket. “mistake. wrong pocket.”"], ["i spread the notes on the table. i line them by size, not truth. “one label,” i say. i keep the contradiction in the middle. i pocket the smallest note. “pattern, maybe.”", "i rub my greasy fingertips together. “one label,” i 